Prusa Research pioneered open-source 3D printer design with fully modular, user-repairable architecture. All replacement parts are available for purchase from their store, with comprehensive assembly manuals and 3D-printable plastic component alternatives. The company publishes CAD files and firmware under open-source licenses, enabling users to customize, upgrade, and self-repair devices. This design philosophy extends device lifespan significantly, reducing e-waste in the maker and manufacturing communities. Prusa offers long-term spare parts availability and comprehensive documentation for devices no longer in production.